# Ⅱ. THE CYBER LANGUAGES — COMPLETE HIERARCHY

```
LAYER 0: BINARY (Yin-Yang, 0/1)
    │
    ├─ LAYER 0.5: HARDWARE DESCRIPTION (VHDL, Verilog)
    │
    ├─ LAYER 1: ASSEMBLY (x86, ARM, MIPS, RISC-V)
    │
    ├─ LAYER 2: SYSTEMS LANGUAGES
    │   ├─ C (Latin of computing)
    │   ├─ C++ (Greek extension)
    │   ├─ Rust (Sanskrit precision)
    │   └─ Go (Stoic simplicity)
    │
    ├─ LAYER 3: APPLICATION LANGUAGES
    │   ├─ Python (Demotic accessibility)
    │   ├─ JavaScript (Phoenician spread)
    │   ├─ TypeScript (Sanskrit strictness) ← KEY FINDING
    │   ├─ Java (Roman institution)
    │   ├─ C# (Microsoft Latin)
    │   └─ Swift (Apple's modern C)
    │
    ├─ LAYER 4: SPECIALIZED LANGUAGES
    │   ├─ SQL (Relational data)
    │   ├─ Haskell (Pure functional/Platonic)
    │   ├─ Lisp (Symbolic AI)
    │   ├─ Prolog (Aristotelian logic)
    │   └─ R (Statistics)
    │
    ├─ LAYER 5: BLOCKCHAIN/DECENTRALIZED
    │   ├─ Motoko (ICP native) ← MMS SUBSTRATE
    │   ├─ Solidity (Ethereum)
    │   ├─ Rust (Solana)
    │   └─ Move (Aptos)
    │
    └─ LAYER 6: MARKUP/CONFIG
        ├─ HTML (Structure)
        ├─ CSS (Style)
        ├─ JSON (Data)
        └─ GraphQL (Query)
```

